⍝ AllPrimitives.tc
⍝ ════════════════

∇ON_ERROR ARGS;N;A;B;X;OPER;FH;LINES;TS;NAME;FMT
 ⍝ write /tmp/ALL_PRIMITIVES_ERROR_N.apl: a self-contained script that
 ⍝ reconstructs A, B, X (via 10 ⎕CR) and then executes OPER, so the
 ⍝ failure captured in ARGS←(N A B X OPER) can be reproduced later.
 ⍝
 (N A B X OPER)←ARGS
 NAME←'/tmp/ALL_PRIMITIVES_ERROR_',(⍕N),'.apl'
 FH←'w' ⎕FIO.fopen NAME
 FMT←'%s',(⎕UCS 10)
 TS←⎕TS
 ⊣((⊂FMT),⊂'⍝ ',(⍕TS[1]),'-',(⍕TS[2]),'-',(⍕TS[3]),' ',(⍕TS[4]),':',(⍕TS[5]),':',(⍕TS[6])) ⎕FIO.fprintf FH
 LINES←(10⎕CR 'A'),(10⎕CR 'B'),(10⎕CR 'X'),⊂OPER
 ⊣{⊣((⊂FMT),⊂⍵) ⎕FIO.fprintf FH}¨LINES
 ⊣⎕FIO.fclose FH
∇

∇Z←ALL_PRIMITIVES SECONDS; ⎕IO;T0;PRIM;TD;RE;A;B;X;ROW;OPER;EXPD;RC;ET;RES;LCNT;ECNT;RC2;ET2;RES2;SEED;RCG;ETG;RESG;FPOOL
 ⍝ run for SECONDS seconds
 ⍝
 ⍝ B is generated first; A_stim="~B" (set for rval.def rows whose Z
 ⍝ constraint requires (⍴A)⌈⍴B, i.e. scalar-extension pairs like A+B)
 ⍝ then calls 7 ⎕RVAL B to conform A to B (scalar or exactly ⍴B) instead
 ⍝ of generating A independently and hoping it happens to fit.
 ⍝ TODO: many other primitives (replicate A/B, reshape A⍴B, encode/decode
 ⍝ A⊤B/A⊥B, catenate, ...) still need their own per-primitive conforming
 ⍝ rule in ⎕RVAL; for now they keep generating A independently.
 ⍝
 SEED←(8⍴256)⊤((⎕TS[3]-1)×24×60×60×1000)+24 60 60 1000⊥⎕TS[4 5 6 7]
 ⊣0 ⎕RVAL SEED       ⍝ seed from current time so different runs differ
 RE←10000            ⍝ desired ⍴∈ limit (⎕RVAL nesting budget fixed, SVN r2037)
 TD ← 15 70 15 5 5   ⍝ desired type distribution
 PRIM←6 ⎕RVAL ⍬
 FPOOL←'+-×⌈⌊'       ⍝ scalar dyadic (also valid monadic) functions for f/g placeholders
 T0←24 60 60⊥⎕TS[4 5 6]
 LCNT←0              ⍝ number of loop iterations so far
 ECNT←0              ⍝ number of ERROR: exits so far
 A←⍬ ◊ B←⍬ ◊ X←⍬ ◊ OPER←''   ⍝ safe defaults so ON_ERROR never sees undefined names
LOOP:
 LCNT←LCNT+1
 ⊣⎕DL 0.1   ⍝ rate limit (unconditional: caps load on server72 every iteration)
 ROW←PRIM[?≢PRIM;]      ⍝ pick a random primitive: arity A_stim B_stim X_stim Z_constraint
 (OPER EXPD)←ROW[1 5]   ⍝ arity expression (e.g. Z←A+B) and Z constraint, set first so
                        ⍝ ON_ERROR always has a valid OPER even if generation fails below
 OPER[⍸OPER='f']←FPOOL[?(+/OPER='f')⍴5]   ⍝ operator-taking primitives (f/,f¨,f.g,...):
 OPER[⍸OPER='g']←FPOOL[?(+/OPER='g')⍴5]   ⍝ substitute a real function for the placeholder(s)
                                          ⍝ (?N already respects ⎕IO — no +1 needed)
 ⍝ B is generated first, so that A (and X) can conform to B's ACTUAL
 ⍝ shape/rank instead of being generated independently and hoping they
 ⍝ happen to fit (per SVN r2037 discussion: fix this inside ⎕RVAL, not
 ⍝ by post-hoc patching in this function).
 ⍝
 (RCG ETG RESG)←⎕EC '{⎕RVAL⍣(0<≢⍵)⊢⍵}⍎3⊃ROW'
 →(RCG≠1)/ERROR         ⍝ generation itself failed (e.g. a bad rval.def stim)
 B←RESG
 →(~(2⊃ROW)≡'~B')/NORMALA
 (RCG ETG RESG)←⎕EC '7 ⎕RVAL B'   ⍝ A_stim="~B": conform to B (scalar or ⍴B)
 →GOTA
NORMALA:
 (RCG ETG RESG)←⎕EC '{⎕RVAL⍣(0<≢⍵)⊢⍵}⍎2⊃ROW'   ⍝ still independent for other primitives
GOTA:
 →(RCG≠1)/ERROR
 A←RESG
 (RCG ETG RESG)←⎕EC '{⎕RVAL⍣(0<≢⍵)⊢⍵}⍎4⊃ROW'
 →(RCG≠1)/ERROR
 X←RESG
 ⍝ X_stim is still generated independently of B, with no idea what B's
 ⍝ actual rank turned out to be — that produced axis values with no
 ⍝ relation to B at all (observed: values like 7509335927660159858,
 ⍝ causing WS FULL in e.g. ⊃[X]B). Every axis-taking primitive in
 ⍝ rval.def is [X]B, so derive a valid axis from B's real rank instead,
 ⍝ when one is wanted (X_stim non-empty) and B actually has axes.
 →((0=≢X)∨0=≢⍴B)/NOAXIS
 X←?≢⍴B
NOAXIS:
 (RC ET RES)←⎕EC OPER   ⍝ execute OPER; on success (RC=2) RES is the value OPER returned
 →(RC≠2)/ERROR          ⍝ OPER itself failed (e.g. non-conforming random A/B)
 (RC2 ET2 RES2)←⎕EC EXPD     ⍝ evaluate the invariant; a plain expr gives RC=1 on success
 →(RC2≠1)/ERROR              ⍝ the constraint expression itself failed to evaluate
 →(RES2)/LOOP                ⍝ invariant holds: keep fuzzing
 ⍝ invariant violated here — falls through (handling TBD)
 →((24 60 60⊥⎕TS[4 5 6]) < T0 + SECONDS)/LOOP
 Z←1 ◊ →0
ERROR:
 ECNT←ECNT+1
 ON_ERROR ECNT A B X OPER   ⍝ dump a reproducer for each of the first 10 errors
 →(ECNT<10)/LOOP            ⍝ keep fuzzing until the 10th error
 Z←0
∇

      ALL_PRIMITIVES 5
1

      )CHECK BRIEF
